{"name":"Cashew Cheese","hex":"#fcf9bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cashew","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any tree of the genus Anacardium.","A tree, Anacardium occidentale, native to northeastern Brazil, now widely grown in tropical climates for its cashew nuts and cashew apples."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cashew"},{"term":"cheese","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dairy product made from curdled or cultured milk.","Any particular variety of cheese."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To prepare curds for making cheese.","To make holes in a pattern of circuitry to decrease pattern density."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheese"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cashew","blocks":[{"text":"Cashew is the common name of a tropical evergreen tree Anacardium occidentale, in the family Anacardiaceae. It is the source of the cashew nut and the cashew apple. The tree can grow as tall as 14 meters."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Cashew_apples.jpg/330px-Cashew_apples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cashew","wikidata":"Q34007"},{"title":"Cheese","blocks":[{"text":"Cheese is a type of dairy product produced in a range of flavors, textures, and forms by curdling of milk, usually from cows, goats or sheep, and sometimes of water buffalo. During production, milk is usually acidified and either the enzymes of rennet or bacterial enzymes with similar activity are added to cause the protein casein to coagulate. The solid curds, consisting of proteins and milkfat, are then separated from the liquid whey and pressed into finished cheese. Some cheeses have aromatic molds on the outer layer or rind, while others have them throughout."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/Cheese_platter.jpg/330px-Cheese_platter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=